    honestNote:
      'Every quoted line is his, from the recording of The Debating Spirit of Strife, with the minute and second given; the adversary’s name is written lowercase in our text whatever the transcript’s case. The rest of his argument is told as summary and marked as his. Two parts of the sermon are summarized without detail: a story in which he publicly connected an anonymous critic to a fraternity and called it a pledge to a false god, and accounts he says he heard in Nigeria from former practitioners of witchcraft about using social media to reach people; the first is an accusation against a private person and is left out, and the second is told as his report, weighed by what the Word says of real spiritual darkness and of Christ’s authority over it. Where he applies Revelation-era or Egyptian-myth arguments the lesson weighs them by the Word.',
