      'Pastor Darby taught that what the world calls victim psychology the Word would call emotional witchcraft: using your emotions to control someone else’s, through manipulation, intimidation and domination. Drawing on Martha in Luke 10, he showed how a person who takes on what nobody asked of her, and then is not applauded, turns the hurt into blame and appeals for pity to control others. He said such a person never sees himself as the one doing harm, consumes people instead of enjoying them, and holds others hostage; and he insisted that even those who have truly been wronged, as Black Americans have been, must break the habit by going to the cross and saying, it is me.',
